 ### Improved Quadratic Taylor Inclusion Function
-An improved inclusion function that enforces constraints from both first-order ($\lambda$) and second-order ($\gamma$) Lipschitz constants. It behaves as a regular quadratic bound as long as its derivative is within $[-\lambda, \lambda]$, switching to a linear bound otherwise to prevent the quadratic term from growing too fast and providing loose bounds. [Link](1902-improved-quadratic-taylor-inclusion-function.md)
