 ### Forward Linear Inclusion Function
-A simpler inclusion function using only the first derivative and a first-order Lipschitz constant. It is less accurate for curved surfaces but cheaper to compute and does not suffer from the exponential $\gamma$ growth in the same way. [Link](1901-forward-linear-inclusion-function.md)
