 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per step for the bound calculation itself, but requires computing the gradient $F_n'(t_0)$, which is $O(n)$ for $n$ octaves if computed naively, or optimized via BVH.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per step.
-- **Measured Performance:** On the "Sponge" scene without enhancements, Regular Quad bounds have 599.9 avg steps, 8969.0 avg octaves, and 181.8 ms time, resulting in a $\times 0.6$ speedup (slowdown) vs Linear bounds (ref). On the "Sponge (far)" scene, they have 416.6 avg steps, 4671.5 avg octaves, and 96.2 ms time, resulting in a $\times 0.4$ slowdown vs Linear bounds [S1].
