 ## Background
-Quadratic Taylor Inclusion Functions were introduced by Aydinlilar et al. in the context of fast sphere tracing of procedural volumetric noise [S1]. The method leverages the quadratic Taylor expansion to create forward inclusion functions that bound the implicit function's value along a ray. The approach was developed to address the inefficiency of linear bounds for grazing rays and to exploit the smoothness of derivatives in procedural noise functions [S1].
